-- title:
--   Freeness over the transposed integer subalgebra in characteristic zero
-- statement:
--   Let $\iota$ be a type, let $n,d$ be natural numbers, and let $M\colon \iota \to M_n(\mathbb{Z})$ be a family of integer matrices that commute pairwise, $M_iM_j = M_jM_i$ for all $i,j$. For a commutative ring $R$ write $A_R$ for the $R$-subalgebra of $M_n(R)$ generated by the set of entrywise images of the $M_i$ under the canonical map $\mathbb{Z}\to R$, and $A_R^{t}$ for the $R$-subalgebra generated by the entrywise images of the transposes $M_i^{T}$. Two hypotheses are imposed over $\mathbb{C}$: first, there exist vectors $v_1,\dots,v_d \in \mathbb{C}^n$ such that the map $A_{\mathbb{C}}^{d} \to \mathbb{C}^n$, $(c_1,\dots,c_d)\mapsto \sum_k c_k v_k$ (each $c_k$ acting on $v_k$ by matrix–vector multiplication), is bijective; second, for every $\mathbb{C}$-algebra homomorphism $\chi\colon A_{\mathbb{C}} \to \mathbb{C}$ the intersection over all $a \in A_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the eigenspaces of the endomorphism of $\mathbb{C}^n$ given by $a$ for the eigenvalue $\chi(a)$ has $\mathbb{C}$-dimension exactly $d$. The conclusion is that for every field $K$ of characteristic zero there exist vectors $w_1,\dots,w_d \in K^n$ for which the map $(A_K^{t})^{d} \to K^n$, $(c_1,\dots,c_d)\mapsto \sum_k c_k w_k$, is bijective; that is, $K^n$ is free of rank $d$ over the subalgebra generated by the transposed matrices.
--
--   This is the piece of linear algebra that converts freeness of rank $d$ of a column module over a commuting family of integer matrices, known over $\mathbb{C}$ together with the statement that each eigencharacter occurs with multiplicity $d$, into freeness of rank $d$ of the dual (transposed) module over an arbitrary field of characteristic zero. It is used in the construction of a basis of the rational Tate module of the Jacobian of a modular curve over its Hecke algebra, where the input over $\mathbb{C}$ comes from the Eichler–Shimura description of parabolic cohomology.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Matrix_exists_bijective_transpose_mulVec_of_adjoin_intCast.lean

